WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.763
Welcome.

2
00:00:00.763 --> 00:00:04.732
This briefing comes from Compliance
Automation and Day-Two Operations,

3
00:00:04.732 --> 00:00:07.775
one of the books of the
Federal Modernization Workbook.

4
00:00:07.775 --> 00:00:11.330
It's written for CIOs, service
desk and operations leads,

5
00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:14.113
and information system security officers.

6
00:00:14.113 --> 00:00:15.526
I'll take four questions.

7
00:00:15.526 --> 00:00:19.038
Why does modernization succeed
or fail at the help desk?

8
00:00:19.038 --> 00:00:20.625
What does day two run on?

9
00:00:20.625 --> 00:00:21.537
Who runs it?

10
00:00:21.537 --> 00:00:23.801
And how do you run it, and prove it works?

11
00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:25.350
The short version is this.

12
00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:28.050
Cutover proves the new
estate can be built.

13
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:32.050
The first locked-out user on Monday
morning proves whether it can be run.

14
00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:35.110
Let's start with why the
help desk holds the keys.
